    "body": "<h2 id=\"h_01JDJ01PRM9JWAXQBYSFR1FTYN\">You will learn</h2>\n<p>Learn how to update the credit card information associated with your account. Note that Klaviyo does not support multiple credit cards in a single account.</p>\n<p>This guide will help you edit or change the payment method for your Klaviyo account. To remove your card, you must make changes to your plan. See <a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/1260805595309\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">how to downgrade to free, cancel a plan, or close your Klaviyo account</a>. </p>\n<h2 id=\"h_01JDJ01PRM0XRVXCASG20DB87K\">Before you begin</h2>\n<p>If a payment fails, Klaviyo will automatically initiate <a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/12557377520027\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">a retry process</a>. In cases where there are multiple failed payments, your account will be temporarily suspended. This suspension indicates that an update to your credit card information may be necessary.</p>\n<p>Once you update your card and the overdue payment is successfully processed, your account will be automatically re-enabled.</p>\n<div class=\"bs-callout bs-callout-default\">\n<p>Klaviyo may take up to 1 hour to attempt processing the new card, resulting in a potential delay before your account's status updates. We recommend checking back after this 1 hour period. If your account is not yet re-enabled, <a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/115001002272\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">contact our support team for assistance</a>.</p>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"h_01JDJ01PRM394HZFZR5V3XXQWX\">Update your credit card information </h2>\n<div class=\"bs-callout bs-callout-default\">\n<p>When adding or updating a credit card, please ensure the card is linked to a valid zip code (also called a \"postal code\"). The zip code you provide must match the one associated with the card. Keep in mind that the card's postal code may differ from your <a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/1260805043069\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">organization's billing address</a>. </p>\n</div>\n<ol>\n<li>In Klaviyo, click your organization name in the bottom left corner.</li>\n<li>Select <strong>Billing</strong>.<br><img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/31422136288923\" alt=\"orgname1.jpg\">\n</li>\n<li>In the <em>Overview </em>tab, go to the <em>Billing </em>section.</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Update billing</strong>.<strong><br><img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/31422153000987\" alt=\"credit2.jpg\"><br></strong>\n</li>\n<li>Add in your:\n<ol>\n<li>Card number</li>\n<li>Expiration date</li>\n<li>Security code (CVC number)</li>\n<li>Country</li>\n<li>ZIP code<br><img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/31422136289819\" alt=\"credit3.jpg\">\n</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Update billing</strong>.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"h_01JDJ561BQX83DZ2M5A7BXM9KG\">Next steps</h2>\n<p>Once you've updated your card, <a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/1260805043069\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">change your billing address to match the new card</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"h_01JDJ01PRMZTA0NH4S84PDFVJN\">Additional resources</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/115000976672\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Understand how Klaviyo billing works </a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/115005251028\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Why is my account disabled?</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/115001002272\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">How to contact support</a></li>\n</ul>",
    "user_segment_ids": []
  },
